WEBVTT

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.100
What kind of work do you do, Dad?

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.500
Well, you see...

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.210
I make everyone's lives a little bit easier.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.540
My work brings us closer to a better future.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.510
It must be pretty amazing!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.380
That's right. It's amazing.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:25.550
But to make it happen, sacrifices must be made.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.690
D-Dad?

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.090
Why?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.140
What the heck, Dad?

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.580
Why?

00:00:51.950 --> 00:01:01.890
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:11.890
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:22.280
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:32.280
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:42.450
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.980
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:01:52.980 --> 00:02:02.970
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.650
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.880
Shun? It's time for lunch!

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.310
Shun?

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:35.750
In the end, all we did was hurt him.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.980
We knew this would happen...

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.390
Emilio? Shall we eat without him?

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.570
I'm coming in.

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.030
Makiko worked hard to make this.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.430
You should eat it.

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.940
What the heck?

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:03.910
If that's all you came for, get out already.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:06.880
I'll leave as soon as I see you eat this.

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:11.850
Emilio.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.220
What?

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.720
I...

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.760
I never understood why you wanted to kill Delzaine so much.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:26.040
How you could ever hate your own father enough to want to kill him.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.970
But now...

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:32.710
Now that I'm in your shoes, I know how you feel.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.580
Knowing all the lies he's told me...

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.610
It's messing with my head.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.880
I'm no different than--

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.150
You are different.

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.590
Emilio?

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.660
Eat all of your lunch.

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.290
Your mom knows how to cook.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:54.060
She's better than all the chefs in the castle.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:02.340
"21: Confrontation"

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.980
From Guidoro and the others?

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.620
Yeah.

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:23.990
It was a field report... and a few complaints about his companions.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:28.860
Hopefully they all get along by the time they get back.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:30.200
Let's hope.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.600
It seems they've tracked down Ibelda as well.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.670
Really?

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.200
Oh! There you are! Demetrio!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.480
We know what happened to Emilio and Shun!

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.780
What happened?

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.350
Those two disappeared somewhere in the castle's dungeon.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:47.180
Dungeon?

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.890
Yes. One guard saw Emilio and
Shun heading into the dungeons.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.320
There's been no trace of them since.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.060
Shun once said the dungeons were where he first appeared.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.230
Scour the dungeons again.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:03.370
Sure!

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.870
I'll help as well.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.470
Please.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:07.400
Demetrio.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:08.840
Eljuia?

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.140
Allow me to act on my own.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.380
I want to look into something.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.750
What is it?

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:21.720
I had another vision of Endora's destruction this morning.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:25.090
Does it have to do with the abnormal Warp Particles?

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.820
Yes.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:31.730
My family possesses a special talent of perception.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.260
If I use it to its fullest potential,

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:38.000
I may be able to see the reason behind this imbalance.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:50.110
Letters are appearing!

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.550
Then we were right.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.750
Excellent work, Joseph.

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.250
Indeed! But this is all thanks to Professor Pascal!

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:03.190
According to your research thesis, people can only see a portion of the wavelengths in light.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:08.600
Using a chemical reaction, we can recover these letters that are faded with age.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:09.730
Yeah, right.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:15.240
We sure are lucky that Rodney here held onto these old books for us.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:19.380
I'm glad to say my tendency to hoard things finally paid off.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:21.540
Now, shall we see what we find?

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:23.750
Please.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.210
Call Asanaga for me.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:27.880
He's in a meeting. Please, sit down.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:29.550
This is important!

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.150
Please!

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:34.120
This is no place for kids to play.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.620
Please leave.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.830
Listen to me! I--

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.960
Let go of me! I need to talk with Asanaga!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.400
Let me meet with Asanaga!

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:43.960
What is this ruckus?

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.600
Asanaga!

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:48.140
It's you again?

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.770
I thought it might have been Shun.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.400
I came to talk with you about him.

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.110
Escort him to my office.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.020
I'm very sorry.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.920
I'm sure you don't like facing such a weapon.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:09.020
But see, I value my own life as well.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.690
You're not sorry.

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:14.130
Not you, who brought Endora to its knees.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.470
So, what have you come for?

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:19.260
I have no interest in you.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.970
Let me ask once more.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:26.040
You said you killed my father. Was that true?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.640
Yes, it was.

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:31.210
It was I who killed Alzerm Langheim.

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:34.450
I won't try to hide it. There's no reason to.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.150
Alzerm was simply not fit to be a king.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.290
What?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.790
His ambition was swayed by a few sweet words.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.290
His mind was shallow and weak.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.990
And not just that...

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:52.370
The persecution of Zoozians and others only worsened under his rule.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:54.340
Did you not know?

00:07:54.340 --> 00:08:00.880
With Delzaine becoming king,
Endora should have improved to an extent.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.310
It can't be...

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:06.480
In fact, did Delzaine not die for your sake?

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.050
Let me ask...

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.750
Ask what?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:16.530
Your son... Do you really love Shun?

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.690
Yes, I love him.

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:22.530
Even if he's not my blood, Shun is still my son.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:26.770
Ever since the beginning, I've loved him dearly.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.340
You see... I don't wish to argue with Shun.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:37.250
I want him to understand what I'm doing so that we can live together and move forward as a family.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:39.450
That's what I'm hoping.

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.780
To me, that child is truly irreplaceable.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:49.690
As long as you don't get in our way,
I don't intend to harm you.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:52.460
As long as you don't get in my way.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.740
How long are you going to sulk for?

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.140
Emilio...

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:16.310
I just went and met with your father.

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.590
You... He almost killed you before!

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.460
Weren't you in danger?

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:24.490
I wanted to confirm something.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.600
What do you mean?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:30.050
Asanaga said that he loved you.

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:36.240
That even though you're not his blood, that you're his own son.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.580
That he wants to move forward with you as a family.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:41.110
But...

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:42.410
I...

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:45.950
In the end, I couldn't make peace with Delzaine.

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.320
Emilio...

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:50.490
I hated him with a passion all on my own.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:51.820
As a result...

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.260
...it couldn't have ended any worse.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.690
Shun, don't make that mistake. Don't do it.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.660
Go to Asanaga...

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.130
Go to your father and talk.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:06.600
Listen to what he says, and then decide.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.710
Don't think about my father or me.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.470
Think about what you want for yourself and decide.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.640
You're right.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.680
I... I'm going to talk with him.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.850
If I don't, nothing will change.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:28.020
Thank you, Emilio.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:30.960
I don't deserve any thanks.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.830
You need to be more honest.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:50.480
What's the deal with assembling us all?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.580
We understand much more now.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:55.150
Everyone needs to know.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.490
Though Eljuia seems to be missing...

00:10:57.490 --> 00:10:59.860
He's closed himself in a room.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:03.850
He's doing a ritual of some sorts to raise his awareness.

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:08.230
He said he's not eating until the ritual is over.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:10.570
Will he be okay?

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.930
I'm sure he's fine.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.600
All we can do is trust him now.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.210
Pascal. Go ahead when you're ready.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:18.110
Sure.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:23.270
To put it plainly, we've discovered a method to travel between Endora and the surface.

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:28.040
It's likely how Shun ended up here in Endora.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.220
"Dad

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.220
No Subject

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.220
I'll be there at 3:30"

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.760
This place...

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.460
...it used to be where my dad worked.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:44.200
It all started in this little workshop.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:47.600
When I was young, I always used to come here.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.050
Sorry, Shun. The meeting ran long.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.880
No, it's okay.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:06.120
I know you're working real hard to help everybody.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.890
Thanks, Shun.

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:09.790
Shall we go?

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.760
Isn't today your regular inspection?

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.000
I hate the hospital...

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.300
It's so you don't get sick again.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.570
No one uses this place anymore?

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:21.600
Right.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:26.140
The facilities and equipment here can't even compare to the other building.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.580
I see...

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:30.250
But he's left it intact all this time?

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:33.680
Maybe this place has some special meaning to Asanaga.

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.780
Shun. Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:39.450
You came, too?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:43.360
I only came to hear what Shun has to say.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.520
I don't plan to intervene.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.700
You don't look well, Shun.

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:56.100
I never wanted to see you suffer.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:59.610
I don't know what to think anymore.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:02.210
I know I don't hate you, Dad.

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:05.350
You're obsessed with work, but you're kind, too.

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.980
But...

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:10.950
You killed Emilio's father and tore Endora apart.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:14.560
What were you thinking?! What are you after?!

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.490
What's my reason?

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:17.890
Indeed...

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.570
Dad? That's...

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.300
Parinblue.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:33.680
A spatial transition device that allows movement between Endora and the surface.

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:38.250
It's a specimen of ancient super-technology that Makiko discovered.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.250
The creation of Endora is shrouded in mystery.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:48.660
Legends and fables suggest it may have been fashioned by other beings from some distant planet.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:52.890
Oh! I heard stories like that when I was little!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:53.860
Yes...

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:59.570
One piece of technology they may have left behind was called a "parinblue."

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:06.370
But when the link between Endora and the surface was severed, the majority of them were broken.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:11.050
It appears to operate with an impulse to the heart.

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:17.020
For example, whether that's anger, fear, or even passion and intense curiosity.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:21.090
It takes the body and disassembles it into countless particles.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.360
Then to reform it in an alternate space--

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.790
Let's skip the technicalities for now.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:30.030
In any case, Shun came to Endora through the power of a parinblue.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.740
It also explains how he vanished to the surface.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:36.570
Can Emilio and Shun come back home?

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:40.780
As long as they possess the parinblue, it should be possible.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:43.040
Though, I can't say for certain.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:49.050
Are you telling me that Shun has held onto one of those parinblue this entire time?

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:51.790
He never said even a single word about it.

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.390
He may have not known about it himself.

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:58.330
My guess is that the parinblue is inside of Shun.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:00.630
You're saying there's one inside me?

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:05.830
When you touched the parinblue kept secure in my office, it was absorbed inside you.

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:10.610
That's why you're able to go between Endora and the surface.

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:16.010
For years, I've studied phenomenon regarding the underground world.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.310
Through my work, I realized something.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:23.150
Endora possesses a source of energy not found on the surface.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.520
Warp Particles...

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.520
That's right.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:31.360
If we could harness that on the surface, it would make everyone's lives here better.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.830
You understand that, right?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.170
That is why I went to Endora.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.970
To obtain Warp Particles for our use through whatever means.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.540
And you would kill people for it?!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:48.180
Have not many wars been fought over some resource?

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:52.510
That is the extent of how valuable
Warp Particles really are.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:59.120
Even now, we tap Warp Particles from Endora to produce a supply here on the surface.

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:02.390
Thanks to that, our lives have become bountiful

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:06.330
and our energy and pollution problems have been lessened.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.630
Isn't that a wonderful thing?

00:16:09.630 --> 00:16:11.470
Don't you understand, Shun?

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:16.340
This solution is more important than one life... or even one country.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:21.040
Once upon a time, you, too, believed that my work was amazing.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.380
But...

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:28.820
And what's more, Shun...
It was for your own sake, too.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.220
Huh?

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:46.840
You were ill from a pandemic that was untreatable in Endora.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.040
I... know that.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:53.040
That's why you took me to the surface to be treated in a hospital.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.680
It takes money to pay for those treatments.

00:16:55.680 --> 00:17:01.880
Even after you were cured, your body was so weak, you were always in the hospital.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:03.620
For my sake...

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:09.720
If I hadn't used Warp Particles to succeed in work,
I'd have never been able to pay those bills.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:12.750
I did it all to protect you.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:15.930
But, Endora...

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.130
Shun, you're too kind a person.

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:24.270
You worry too much about the crumbling kingdom of Endora.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.780
Endora will not last much longer.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:32.450
When the Warp Particles diminish, that world will be unable to sustain its form.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:36.150
So there's no point in even thinking about it anymore.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.720
W-Wait a sec!

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:38.990
What?

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.390
What's that about?

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:43.830
Aren't you the one draining out their Warp Particles?!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.060
That's right.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.830
Well, make it stop!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.560
What are you talking about?

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:49.900
There's no way I'd stop.

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.170
Why not?!

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.070
Did I not just explain?

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:56.670
Warp Particles have had a great influence on the surface.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:18:00.110
Why stop when it has improved so many people's lives?

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:04.510
Do the people of Endora not count as people to you?!

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.480
Yes, that's right.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:14.490
Endora served as a valuable asset to advance humanity.

00:18:14.490 --> 00:18:15.860
Is that not enough?

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:19.630
You'll be the one to continue my work, Shun.

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:20.630
But...

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.800
Yes, there's nothing to worry about.

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:29.100
I'm close to perfecting a system to recycle
Warp Particles and give us an infinite supply.

00:18:29.100 --> 00:18:34.140
Even after Endora has collapsed, we'll have enough reserves to work with forever.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.840
That's not it!

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.180
What?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:39.550
You're sacrificing everyone in Endora?

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.110
I can't let that happen!

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:46.650
Has your time in Endora made you so attached to the place?

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:49.620
Even after such a short time?

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:53.820
In the end, perhaps you belong in Endora and not here.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:59.200
Shun. I cannot allow even you to hold me back.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:03.040
If you won't cooperate, at least stay out of my way.

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:06.980
I would like to avoid having to kill you.

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.530
Enough, Asanaga!

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.810
You bastard!

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:17.320
Emilio!

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:19.250
Emilio! Are you all right?

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.690
I'm not going to shoot you, Shun.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:25.860
You're my precious son.

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:27.860
Stop this, Dad!

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:30.930
Was it you who changed my son?

00:19:30.930 --> 00:19:32.600
How annoying.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:34.670
How very annoying!

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:39.340
If he hadn't met you,
Shun would have followed in my steps!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.080
That's bullshit.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:44.950
Given the circumstances, you better shut your mouth.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:48.880
It's you. You're the nuisance standing in my way!

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:54.620
Stop it!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:20.710
Felix! Hold still!

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.550
You're in the way!

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:30.890
There's too many!

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.490
Any longer and we're in trouble, Guidoro!

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:34.930
I know that!

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.480
Ouch...

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.150
This is...

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.020
It can't be!

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:01.460
Endora?!

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.860
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:13.700
<i>I've walked very far, so far</i>

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:23.200
<i>And I'll walk even farther from here</i>

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:46.000
<i>I don't wish for everything to stay the same</i>

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:56.000
<i>Because change is what got me to where I am</i>

00:21:56.640 --> 00:22:05.190
<i>We've walked very far, so far</i>

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:13.760
<i>We'll go farther than anyone's gone before</i>

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:22.340
<i>Each of us can change the world</i>

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:31.510
<i>That's why I smile at you</i>

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:39.880
"Episode 22: Crisis"

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.720
Next episode, "Crisis."
